  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "line_001",
      "speaker_id": "98124b23-e331-473a-989c-d39c8eba66dd",
      "text": "Hey Maya, I've been trying to revamp my morning routine lately, but I always seem to run out of time before I can even squeeze in a decent breakfast.",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "morning routine",
          "decent breakfast"
        ],
        "idioms": [],
        "grammar_point": "Present Perfect Continuous"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_002",
      "speaker_id": "cf02048c-e2f1-4bf5-9676-b27a7c024a55",
      "text": "Oh, I feel you. I used to struggle with that constantly until I decided to map out my entire evening the night before. Honestly, prep work is a total game-changer.",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "prep work"
        ],
        "idioms": [
          "game-changer"
        ],
        "grammar_point": "Used to for past habits"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_003",
      "speaker_id": "98124b23-e331-473a-989c-d39c8eba66dd",
      "text": "A game-changer? Really? So what does that look like in practice? Are we talking about packing lunches at midnight, or is it more about mental prep?",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "in practice",
          "mental prep"
        ],
        "idioms": [],
        "grammar_point": "Complex question structure with gerunds"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_004",
      "speaker_id": "cf02048c-e2f1-4bf5-9676-b27a7c024a55",
      "text": "A bit of both, actually! I usually set aside fifteen minutes before hitting the sack to lay out my workout gear and chop some veggies for the next day's meals.",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "workout gear"
        ],
        "idioms": [
          "hitting the sack"
        ],
        "grammar_point": "Gerunds after prepositions"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_005",
      "speaker_id": "98124b23-e331-473a-989c-d39c8eba66dd",
      "text": "That sounds incredibly disciplined. I usually just wind down by scrolling on my phone, which, let's face it, is a terrible habit that ruins my sleep hygiene.",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "terrible habit",
          "sleep hygiene"
        ],
        "idioms": [],
        "grammar_point": "Non-defining relative clauses"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_006",
      "speaker_id": "cf02048c-e2f1-4bf5-9676-b27a7c024a55",
      "text": "Exactly! That blue light will definitely throw off your circadian rhythm. If you can kick that habit, you'll find waking up early is no longer an uphill battle.",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "circadian rhythm",
          "kick that habit"
        ],
        "idioms": [
          "uphill battle"
        ],
        "grammar_point": "First Conditional"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_007",
      "speaker_id": "98124b23-e331-473a-989c-d39c8eba66dd",
      "text": "True. I suppose if I actually get a head start the night before, I won't have to rush through my morning cup of coffee. I want to actually savor it, you know?",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "cup of coffee"
        ],
        "idioms": [
          "get a head start"
        ],
        "grammar_point": "Conditional clauses with hypothetical scenarios"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_008",
      "speaker_id": "cf02048c-e2f1-4bf5-9676-b27a7c024a55",
      "text": "Absolutely, mindfulness is key. Once you establish that solid foundation, the rest of your weekday routine just falls into place naturally.",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [
          "solid foundation",
          "weekday routine"
        ],
        "idioms": [
          "falls into place"
        ],
        "grammar_point": "Time clauses with present tense"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_009",
      "speaker_id": "98124b23-e331-473a-989c-d39c8eba66dd",
      "text": "Well, I'm sold. I'll give this evening prep thing a shot tonight. Let's see if I can actually stick to it this time!",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [],
        "idioms": [
          "give it a shot"
        ],
        "grammar_point": "Future intention with will"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "line_010",
      "speaker_id": "cf02048c-e2f1-4bf5-9676-b27a7c024a55",
      "text": "Do it! Just take it one step at a time, and don't beat yourself up if you slip up occasionally.",
      "language_notes": {
        "collocations": [],
        "idioms": [
          "one step at a time"
        ],
        "grammar_point": "Imperatives for advice and encouragement"
      }
    }
  ],
